12:38.867 --> 12:39.508
[SPEAKER_02]: It's possible.

12:40.795 --> 12:44.076
[SPEAKER_02]: Would that be a prelude to a further invasion?

12:46.276 --> 12:49.457
[SPEAKER_02]: I mean, who would seize the fortress without planning to do more?

12:51.797 --> 12:53.778
[SPEAKER_02]: How will you have us inserted with the Corsair?

12:56.198 --> 12:59.859
[SPEAKER_00]: Paul Rivero will be himself, and he'll be out there as a...

13:00.999 --> 13:06.840
[SPEAKER_02]: I mean like an open broad daylight that will go to the... You are going to be selling, you will be known with the captain.

13:11.637 --> 13:13.779
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't know if anybody will blend in at the fortress.

13:13.819 --> 13:17.242
[SPEAKER_00]: You'll be there to lend your magical help to this.

13:17.442 --> 13:18.363
[SPEAKER_00]: This could be nothing.

13:19.484 --> 13:29.232
[SPEAKER_00]: To be honest with you, Admiral Fairfield currently is in charge of the helm.

13:30.093 --> 13:33.796
[SPEAKER_00]: This is getting a little older, so I may have given the incorrect order.

13:33.876 --> 13:35.778
[SPEAKER_00]: However, we do need to investigate.

13:37.375 --> 13:41.618
[SPEAKER_02]: Has he ever given the incorrect order up to this point in time?

13:46.341 --> 13:46.521
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

13:46.541 --> 13:51.104
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay.

13:51.505 --> 13:53.826
[SPEAKER_02]: Is it a pretext of the Corsair?

13:53.846 --> 13:56.808
[SPEAKER_02]: Is it just a regular stopover?

13:56.908 --> 13:59.410
[SPEAKER_02]: Or is it a pretext of delivering food or supplies?

13:59.820 --> 14:01.720
[SPEAKER_00]: No, you'll be going there in force.

14:01.780 --> 14:03.841
[SPEAKER_00]: This is standard practice, actually.

14:04.201 --> 14:05.861
[SPEAKER_00]: We send warships there all the time.

14:06.162 --> 14:07.142
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, okay.

14:07.542 --> 14:08.722
[SPEAKER_00]: But there'll be a full crew.

14:09.442 --> 14:11.503
[SPEAKER_00]: There'll be 250 marines on board.

14:11.863 --> 14:12.783
[SPEAKER_00]: You'll be a part of that.

14:12.883 --> 14:13.423
[SPEAKER_00]: Marines?

14:15.244 --> 14:17.004
[SPEAKER_02]: You know, soldiers that fight on the water.

14:19.065 --> 14:20.465
[SPEAKER_02]: Light armor so they can swim.

14:20.565 --> 14:21.205
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, I know.

14:21.365 --> 14:28.367
[SPEAKER_00]: Paul, you'll be there to lend the power of Lord Jamis.

14:28.587 --> 14:29.427
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, Lord Jeanne.

14:30.747 --> 14:31.447
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you understand?

14:32.448 --> 14:34.670
[SPEAKER_00]: You're a representative of Florian in this.

14:36.551 --> 14:36.891
[SPEAKER_00]: Got you.

14:37.292 --> 14:38.312
[SPEAKER_00]: We'll be given a writ.

14:40.093 --> 14:44.737
[SPEAKER_00]: What I want you to do is investigate the entire helm.

14:45.577 --> 14:47.939
[SPEAKER_00]: Make sure there are no traitors there.

14:48.119 --> 14:49.480
[SPEAKER_00]: There are no Toli rats there.

14:50.481 --> 14:52.362
[SPEAKER_00]: There are no instigators.

14:54.443 --> 14:55.324
[SPEAKER_00]: And then report to me.

14:55.864 --> 14:56.885
[SPEAKER_00]: Jude, you're with him.

14:56.905 --> 14:58.446
[SPEAKER_00]: I know what that means.

14:58.466 --> 14:59.367
[SPEAKER_00]: You're to protect him.

15:06.475 --> 15:06.755
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay.

15:07.655 --> 15:08.415
[SPEAKER_02]: When do you want us to leave?

15:09.856 --> 15:10.636
[SPEAKER_00]: As soon as possible.

15:11.976 --> 15:13.076
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what the meeting was.

15:14.217 --> 15:14.537
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

15:14.617 --> 15:15.997
[SPEAKER_00]: We are assembling the men right now.

15:16.737 --> 15:17.717
[SPEAKER_00]: We'll leave in two hours.

15:19.518 --> 15:19.758
[SPEAKER_00]: All right.

15:20.478 --> 15:21.558
[SPEAKER_00]: You'll leave sooner than that.

15:21.578 --> 15:24.039
[SPEAKER_00]: You'll leave within an hour, but get your equipment together.

15:25.819 --> 15:26.279
[SPEAKER_01]: It'll be time.

15:28.840 --> 15:29.140
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay.

15:33.602 --> 15:35.423
[SPEAKER_02]: Can I get an extra bottle of wine to take with me?

15:35.563 --> 15:36.863
[SPEAKER_00]: No, you cannot do that, Jude.

15:36.923 --> 15:39.784
[SPEAKER_00]: I need you to be sober when you're on the ship.

15:40.064 --> 15:41.344
[SPEAKER_00]: You are not royalty.

15:41.984 --> 15:47.246
[SPEAKER_02]: Doesn't seem like they're real quick to own you.

15:49.226 --> 15:51.367
[SPEAKER_02]: Quicker to me than you, that's for sure.

15:51.427 --> 15:53.227
[SPEAKER_02]: That's not saying much.

15:54.668 --> 15:55.528
[SPEAKER_02]: I know my value.

16:02.007 --> 16:03.608
[SPEAKER_01]: There's plenty more just like you.

16:04.669 --> 16:05.210
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, really?

16:05.250 --> 16:07.192
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

16:08.533 --> 16:09.854
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't even know what a market is.

16:09.974 --> 16:14.218
[SPEAKER_02]: Apparently, I just need to go down to the market and buy a dark, darker house.

16:15.579 --> 16:17.721
[SPEAKER_00]: All right, so... Darker tone.

16:18.401 --> 16:26.388
[SPEAKER_00]: So... You guys are gonna get your shit together.

16:26.869 --> 16:27.149
[SPEAKER_02]: Yes.

16:28.584 --> 16:29.907
[SPEAKER_00]: Actually, you don't have much to get on there.

16:29.927 --> 16:31.149
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't have much to get on there.

16:31.510 --> 16:32.772
[SPEAKER_02]: I always carry everything on me.

16:33.714 --> 16:34.415
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't know about you.

16:35.297 --> 16:36.319
[SPEAKER_02]: You were switching masks, right?

16:36.339 --> 16:36.479
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

16:36.539 --> 16:37.801
[SPEAKER_02]: What did you come out of this room with?

16:38.563 --> 16:45.275
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll come out of my room with a... Alright, so you get ready to go.

